  {
   "id": "out_export",
   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "detail",
   "quote": "all exported with the stack name prefix",
   "select": "outs",
   "quantifier": "all",
   "cond": {
    "path": "export",
    "op": "regex",
    "value": "(?i)^stack[-:_./]"
   },
   "justify": "the adapter resolves AWS::StackName to stack, and the prompt asks for that prefix"
  },
  {
   "id": "x_runtime",
   "kind": "attr",
   "tier": "extra",
   "select": "fn",
   "cond": {
    "path": "Runtime",
    "op": "regex",
    "value": "^python"
   }
  }
 ],
 "notes": "cr is read from __declared__ because a custom resource's type name is free (Custom::*); gated falsy keeps it to resources the defaults create. out_ns matches a whole quoted output name or GetAtt attribute, so ipv4awsdns01 or NameServer1IPv4 can't stand in for a nameserver name. Output tiers are parallel: returning these values is the point of the custom resource. PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: the prompt says the function can delete the delegation set, but the ground truth's Delete branch never calls delete_reusable_delegation_set, so code_delete keeps what both guarantee: a Delete request is handled."
}
